note.p:
Source: Department of State, Central Files, 656.9813/5–1662. Secret; Niact. Drafted by Tyler, Beaudry, and Rusk;
                    cleared by Rice and McGhee; and approved by Rusk. Repeated priority
                    to The Hague and to USUN.

This telegram did not arrive in Djakarta in time for Jones to use in the May 18 morning meeting with Sukarno, but Jones did make the points to Subandrio on May 19. In both meetings, Sukarno and Subandrio
                    expressed great skepticism of Netherlands intentions. (Telegrams 2036 and 2040
                    from Djakarta, May 18 and 19; ibid., 656.9813/5–1862 and 656.9813/5–1962)
